# Copy to `.env` for local development, and set the same variable in Vercel
# (Project Settings > Environment Variables) for preview and production.
#
# reCAPTCHA v3 SITE key for Firebase App Check. This is the public half of the
# pair and is baked into the built HTML by design — the secret key is only ever
# entered in the Firebase console, never here.
#
# The site is `output: 'static'`, so this is read at BUILD time. Changing it
# requires a redeploy, not just a restart.
#
# Leave it unset and App Check simply is not initialised: the pages log a
# warning and still work, right up until App Check enforcement is switched on in
# the Firebase console, at which point every write starts failing.
PUBLIC_RECAPTCHA_V3_SITE_KEY=
